  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/a9b3ea2fd75ea8cbaac2fcd238fd24cc1838826965a9ac10c4b0ff7dfdb3b4ed.png)\n\nIf each cube represents $1$ cubic unit, what is the volume of the figure?",
  "worked_solution": "The figure consists of $3$ rows, and each row has $7$ cubes.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14132963/assets/f025ff2069417083c52390b5e6dbf886c816bc143075ef9778d87265aacf5a70.png)\n\nSo, there are $7\\times 3=21$ cubes in total.\n\nTherefore, the volume of the figure is $21$ cubic units.",
